      "slug": "do-outlier-decisions-matter",
      "title": "Do outlier treatment decisions matter in meta-analysis?",
      "date": "2026-07-25",
      "summary": "Recomputing 358 behavioral science meta-analyses under five outlier treatments barely moves the mean effect, but changes statistical significance in 11.5% of cases and whether the effect clears a smallest-effect-size threshold in 15.9%, with winsorizing changing conclusions least and DFBETAS most.",
